Ensure SQL Server Agent is Running
Replication relies on SQL Server Agent, so make sure it's enabled on both the Publisher and Subscriber servers.


Run the below to check if sql server agent is enabled on Publisher and Subscriber.
EXEC xp_servicecontrol 'QUERYSTATE', 'SQLServerAgent';


If it's not running, start it manually or with:

EXEC xp_servicecontrol 'START', 'SQLServerAgent';


Enable Replication Features
Run this on the Publisher and Distributor:

EXEC sp_configure 'show advanced options', 1;
RECONFIGURE;
EXEC sp_configure 'Replication Enabled', 1;
RECONFIGURE;


START REPLICATION STEPS


Step 1: Configure the Distributor
Run this on the Distributor Server (usually the same as the Publisher).

EXEC sp_adddistributor @distributor = 'YourDistributorServer', @password = 'YourStrongPassword';


Verify distributor setup:
SELECT * FROM msdb.dbo.MSdistpublishers;


Step 2: Configure the Publisher
Run this on the Publisher Server (the source database).


EXEC sp_addpublication 
    @publication = 'YourPublicationName', 
    @publisher = 'YourPublisherServer',
    @publication_type = 0,  -- 0 = Transactional, 1 = Snapshot, 2 = Merge
    @status = 1,
    @sync_method = 0, 
    @retention = 72, 
    @allow_push = 1, 
    @allow_pull = 1,
    @enabled_for_internet = 0, 
    @immediate_sync = 1;


Verify publication setup:

SELECT * FROM distribution.dbo.MSpublications;

Step 3: Add Articles (Tables to Replicate)
Run this on the Publisher Server, specifying which tables to replicate.


EXEC sp_addarticle 
    @publication = 'YourPublicationName',
    @article = 'YourTableName',
    @source_object = 'YourTableName',
    @type = 'logbased';


To replicate multiple tables, repeat this step for each table.


Verify articles:

SELECT * FROM distribution.dbo.MSarticles;


Step 4: Configure the Subscriber
Run this on the Subscriber Server (destination database).


EXEC sp_addsubscription 
    @publication = 'YourPublicationName',
    @subscriber = 'YourSubscriberServer',
    @destination_db = 'YourSubscriberDatabase',
    @subscription_type = 0, -- 0 = Push, 1 = Pull, 2 = Anonymous
    @sync_type = 'automatic',
    @status = 1;


Verify subscription setup:

SELECT * FROM distribution.dbo.MSsubscriptions;
